    <p class="law-disclaimer"><strong>We manage communities. We don’t practice law.</strong> This is plain-English guidance, not legal advice. Much of Louisiana’s Planned Community Act defers to your own governing documents and applies only where those documents are silent; other provisions apply regardless. Some of these statutes are clearer than others, and legal professionals may disagree about what they require. Before you rely on or act on anything here, run it by your association’s attorney — that’s what we tell the boards we manage.</p>
